<newsitem itemid="44943" id="root" date="1996-09-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Williams lifts H1 profit 11.4 pct to record.</title>
<headline>Williams lifts H1 profit 11.4 pct to record.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.0		   vs 9.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.8		    vs 5.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     114.9		  vs 103.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   877.0		  vs 765.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on first-half pretax profits for Williams Holdings Plc, the UK fire protection, security and building products group, were in a range of 111-118.9 million stg, with the interim dividend predicted to be 5.75 to 5.85 pence a share.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 126.3		  vs 110.0</p>
<p> Interest payable	 11.4		   vs 6.9</p>
<p> Tax charge		 39.0		   vs 34.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  75.9		   vs 69.1</p>
<p> Retained profit	  30.2		   vs 25.2</p>
<p> Pay date		   Oct 11 1996</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 1 1996  </p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
